\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Utapau is a planet in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that is covered in savannahs and vast, wide sinkholes.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"},", inhabit the world, living in sinkholes deep beneath the surface of the planet.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Ships visiting Utapau must be extremely careful- gusts of wind can knock ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," out of the sky, and the narrow sinkholes can make maneuvering difficult during landing.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["30\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Some consider the planet to be little more than a legend, and many believe that Utapau might have been the birthplace of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},".\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Social Sciences"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DC\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RESULT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Two races, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"}," (collectively known as the Utapaun), share the planet in a near-symbiotic relationship.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," are a tall Species with a natural predilection for bureaucracy and oversight, while the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"}," are a short Species who excel as laborers and animal handlers.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["An increase in surface storms drove the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," underground long ago, where they joined their civilization with that of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"},".\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DC\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RESULT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["While safe for visitors, Utapau is a strange world that has been shrouded in mystery for years. Its citizens are welcoming to outsiders, but few travel to the backwater planet or even know of its existence.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The planet's two Species, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"},", live together in a symbiotic relationship. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," are the planet's rulers and administrators, and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"}," are the laborers.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"}," have a good relationship, and the only conflicts on the world are between city-states, not between the two Species.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
